+# Performance history
+
+## UserPromptSubmit read path
+
+The repository does not contain a measured full-recall p95 for the
+`UserPromptSubmit` hook on the adversarial synthetic 30-word vocabulary from
+before the term-selection fix.
+
+The fix was to select at most eight prompt terms by descending IDF before
+querying FTS5, dropping terms absent from the store and, for stores with at
+least 50 records, terms present in more than one third of the records. This
+keeps long posting lists from dominating the synchronous read path.
+
+The repository also does not contain a measured full-recall p95 for that same
+adversarial synthetic 30-word vocabulary after the fix.
+
+The other recorded measurements are not substitutes for those two missing
+numbers: `[H6]` in `research/00-evidence-log.md` measures only the BM25 stage on
+a different corpus (p95 35.53 ms with 24 terms and 8.75 ms with top-8 IDF
+terms), while `[I3]` reports a 4.31 ms full-hook p95 for a 50,000-record
+prototype measurement without identifying it as the adversarial synthetic
+30-word-vocabulary run.
